            <ArticleTitle>[The heart and sexual activity].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1331-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>There has been considerable media attention surrounding the commercialisation of Sildenafil. The advice of cardiologists is often solicited before its prescription because of its potential side effects; the cardiovascular stress due to sexual activity is generally modest, both in normal subjects and coronary patients with, however, important individual variations, the &quot;legitimate&quot; nature of the intercourse seeming to be one of the principal factors. Recent coronary events, poorly controlled hypertension and uncompensated cardiac failure are the main contra-indications; the prescription should be based on the results of maximal exercise stress testing in patients at risk.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
